CUDA Batch Image Processing Project - Install and Run
=====================================================

Prerequisites
-------------
1. Linux environment
2. NVIDIA GPU with CUDA support
3. CUDA toolkit (nvcc available in PATH)
4. Python 3
5. make

Build and Run
-------------
From the repository root:

1. chmod +x run.sh
2. ./run.sh

Manual Commands (optional)
--------------------------
1. Generate input dataset:
   python3 src/generate_dataset.py --output data/input --count 200 --width 256 --height 256

2. Build executable:
   make

3. Run processor:
   ./bin/batch_image_processor data/input data/output

Output Artifacts
----------------
1. Processed image files:
   data/output/processed_*.pgm

2. Execution proof log:
   data/output/run_log.txt
